    1	# Pointwise Ramanujan-spike approximator T_Q(n)
    2	
    3	## Object
    4	
    5	For positive integer N and integer cutoff Q ≥ 1, define the
    6	**Mertens–Ramanujan spike intensity** at level Q,
    7	
    8	```
    9	    M_Q(n) := Σ_{q ≤ Q, q squarefree}  mu(gcd(q, n)) / phi(q / gcd(q, n))
    10	```
    11	
    12	and the **pointwise spike approximator** of chi_P at scale Q,
    13	
    14	```
    15	    T_Q(n) := (pi(N) / N) · M_Q(n).
    16	```
    17	
    18	`mu` is the Möbius function and `phi` is Euler's totient. The right-hand
    19	side depends on n through the divisor structure `gcd(q, n)`, and on the
    20	ambient scale N only through the prefactor `pi(N) / N` (the prime
    21	density on `[1, N]`).
    22	
    23	## Identity used (proven from definitions)
    24	
    25	**Hölder reduction.** For squarefree q and any integer n, let
    26	`d = gcd(q, n)` (then d | q, hence d squarefree). Then
    27	
    28	```
    29	    c_q(n)  =  mu(q/d) · phi(d)        (standard for Ramanujan sums)
    30	    mu(q) · c_q(n) / phi(q)  =  mu(d) / phi(q/d).
    ... (197 more lines)
