    1	# sanity_holder.py — Hölder simplification check
    2	
    3	**One-line check** of the project-internal algebraic identity used in
    4	`spike_pointwise.py`:
    5	
    6	> For squarefree q and any integer n with `d := gcd(q, n)`,
    7	>     mu(q) · c_q(n) / phi(q)  =  mu(d) / phi(q/d).
    8	
    9	`c_q(n)` is the Ramanujan sum, computed directly as
    10	`Σ_{j: gcd(j,q)=1} e^{2πi jn / q}`. The script computes both sides
    11	for every squarefree q ∈ [1, 30] and n ∈ [0, 60] and reports any
    12	mismatch with tolerance `1e-9`.
    13	
    14	## Run
    15	
    16	```
    17	python3 sanity_holder.py
    18	```
    19	
    20	## Output
    21	
    22	```
    23	OK: Hoelder simplification mu(q) c_q(n)/phi(q) = mu(gcd) / phi(q/gcd)
    24	    verified for all squarefree q in [1, 30] and n in [0, 60].
    25	```
    26	
    27	Zero failures. The Hölder simplification used in the closed-form
    28	`M_Q(n) = Σ_{q sqf ≤ Q} mu(gcd(q,n)) / phi(q/gcd(q,n))` is exact.
